Any person desiring to vote in any municipal, general, or special election must: Register as an elector in the manner prescribed by law;

Be a citizen of the State of Georgia and of the United States;

Be at least eighteen (18) years of age;

Be a resident of this (municipality/county); and

Be possessed of all other qualifications prescribed by law:

A. No person who has been convicted of a felony involving moral turpitude may register, remain registered, or vote except upon completion of the sentence.

B. No person who has been judicially determined to be mentally incompetent may register, remain registered, or vote unless the disability has been removed.

Any person who possesses the qualifications of an elector except those concerning age shall be permitted to register to vote if such person will acquire such qualifications within six (6) months after the day of registration; provided, however, that such person shall not be permitted to vote in a primary or election until the acquisition of such qualifications.

